    summary: "The average Liberian-dollar personal loan rate stood at 16.16% in February 2026, three full percentage points above the commercial lending rate of 13.11%. For the thousands of micro-entrepreneurs who borrow on personal terms because their businesses lack the formalization to qualify for commercial credit, the gap is a structural penalty that caps growth before it starts.",
