    title: "Banks Hold L$260 Billion in Deposits — Where Does the Money Go?",
    summary: "Liberian commercial banks held L$260,501 million in deposits included in broad money as of March 2026 — US$1.42 billion at prevailing rates. Yet bank claims on the private sector grew just 1.1% over the same year. The deposits are piling up faster than banks are willing to deploy them.",
